# Text files are stored with LF line endings. Shell scripts keep LF even when checked out on Windows: with CRLF
# line endings they no longer run. So do the files of the fixed build environment, which runs on Linux, also when it
# is started on Windows (tools/reproducible, and .dockerignore, whose lines would no longer match with a CR at the end).
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
tools/reproducible/* text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
